WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.977
Spark SQL does not erase the SQL ideas we already learned.

00:00:03.977 --> 00:00:10.257
Filters, joins, grouping, windows, NULL handling, and row grain still matter.

00:00:10.257 --> 00:00:13.467
What changes is the execution environment.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:19.477
In PostgreSQL, we usually think about one database engine managing tables and indexes.

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:24.752
In Spark, the work may run across many workers and many data partitions.

00:00:24.752 --> 00:00:32.467
That means a correct query can still be expensive if it scans too much data or causes large

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:40.117
shuffles. Connect this idea to a healthcare analytics platform processing large longitudinal event tables.

00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:45.802
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:45.802 --> 00:00:53.627
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:53.627 --> 00:00:59.582
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:59.582 --> 00:01:05.519
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
